    "description": "Japan Electronic Materials Corporation, together with its subsidiaries, develops, manufactures, and sells semiconductor inspection and electron tube parts in Japan, rest of Asia, North America, and Europe. The company offers cantilever type and advanced probe cards; heaters and cathodes for receiving tubes and CRTs; filaments for fluorescent character display tubes; and directly heated cathodes. It also provides color TV displays, including high-definition TV, computer, measurement, and radar displays. In addition, the company is involved in the processing and assembly of heat-resistant metals, such as tungsten and molybdenum. Japan Electronic Materials Corporation was incorporated in 1960 and is headquartered in Amagasaki, Japan."
